--TEST--
`Core\Session::start`'s identifier is optional and is a string, so every call shape reaches the same store question -- `rule:core-api/session-roster` and `rule:http-server/a-session-store-answers-four-operations`
--GET--
under=a-request
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The case answers a request, because every call shape below reaches the store
// question only through the one `start` asks first
// (`rule:security/request-state-throws-in-an-isolate`).
//
// § 1's signature is `start(?tainted string $presented = null)`, and the two
// halves of that are separate claims. The parameter is real — a string call
// site compiles — and the default is real — an omitting one compiles too. A row
// that had declared no parameter would fail the second call below at compile
// time, and one that had declared it required would fail the first, so a member
// answering plausibly on one line still fails here.
//
// What each call *does* is out of reach without a store, so what is asserted is
// that all three reach the same place: the configured-store question, which is
// the first thing `start` asks whatever it was handed.
array<string> $shapes = [
    // The whole width of an identifier this store issues: 22 base64url
    // characters, which is what `mint` renders 128 drawn bits to.
    "PmA5tKz1QvR3sYbNqLwXe2",
    // And one it plainly did not — absence and a forgery are the same answer
    // under § 2, so neither can be told from the other by which error arrives.
    "not-an-identifier",
];
uint $presented = 0;
foreach ($shapes as string $shape) {
    try {
        Core\Session::start($shape);
    } catch (RuntimeError $unconfigured) {
        if (Core\Str::contains($unconfigured->message, "[session] backend")) {
            $presented = $presented + 1;
        }
    }
}
echo "a presented identifier reached the store question ", $presented, " of 2\n";

// The omitted one, which is the ordinary case: the identifier is read from the
// `[session] cookie` field of the request rather than written at the call site.
uint $omitted = 0;
try {
    Core\Session::start();
} catch (RuntimeError $unconfigured) {
    if (Core\Str::contains($unconfigured->message, "[session] backend")) {
        $omitted = $omitted + 1;
    }
}
echo "an omitted identifier reached the same question ", $omitted, " of 1\n";
--EXPECT--
a presented identifier reached the store question 2 of 2
an omitted identifier reached the same question 1 of 1
